ms changed everything]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133402660.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Assateague Island was once planned as a major resort community with thousands of homes, roads and commercial areas. Two powerful storms changed that future. A 1933 hurricane split the island, while the 1962 Ash Wednesday storm destroyed roads and structures. The island was later protected as a National Seashore in 1965, preserving its beaches, wildlife and natural coastal habitats.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-early-1960s-developers-sold-5850-lots-for-a-private-resort-on-assateague-island-one-five-day-storm-wiped-out-nearly-every-house-and-helped-turn-it-into-a-national-seashore/articleshow/133402660.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-early-1960s-developers-sold-5850-lots-for-a-private-resort-on-assateague-island-one-five-day-storm-wiped-out-nearly-every-house-and-helped-turn-it-into-a-national-seashore/articleshow/133402660.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T19:58:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133404183,imgsize-158621.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arizona eighth-grader’s drone study finds rural areas have more ground-level CO2]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133425451.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-luca-mcgill-the-arizona-eighth-grader-who-flew-a-drone-120-metres-into-the-sky-expecting-cities-to-have-the-most-ground-level-co2-rural-areas-did-instead/articleshow/133425451.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-luca-mcgill-the-arizona-eighth-grader-who-flew-a-drone-120-metres-into-the-sky-expecting-cities-to-have-the-most-ground-level-co2-rural-areas-did-instead/articleshow/133425451.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T19:12:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133425540,imgsize-44396.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Rockefeller secretly bought 35,000 acres, then donated them]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133405127.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1927, John D. Rockefeller Jr. quietly began buying large areas of land in Wyoming’s Jackson Hole through the Snake River Land Company. The company concealed Rockefeller’s involvement and eventually acquired more than 35,000 acres for $1.4 million. The land was later donated to the US government and became part of Grand Teton National Park.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1927-john-d-rockefeller-jr-secretly-used-a-shell-company-to-buy-over-35000-wyoming-acres-for-1-4-million-nps-says-acquiring-the-same-amount-of-jackson-hole-land-today-would-cost-over-1-billion/articleshow/133405127.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1927-john-d-rockefeller-jr-secretly-used-a-shell-company-to-buy-over-35000-wyoming-acres-for-1-4-million-nps-says-acquiring-the-same-amount-of-jackson-hole-land-today-would-cost-over-1-billion/articleshow/133405127.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T18:57:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133405756,imgsize-90091.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Good news for family-based Green Card applicants from India in Visa Bulletin September 2026, no relief for employment-based categories]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133425265.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/good-news-for-family-based-indian-green-card-applicants-in-visa-bulletin-september-2026-no-relief-for-employment-based-categories/articleshow/133425265.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/good-news-for-family-based-indian-green-card-applicants-in-visa-bulletin-september-2026-no-relief-for-employment-based-categories/articleshow/133425265.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T18:58:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133425296,imgsize-190834.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Swedish hospital stores winter snow and pumps its meltwater through the building in summer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133400895.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A hospital in Sundsvall, central Sweden, used an unusual cooling system that stored winter snow for use during summer. The snow was kept in a large, insulated storage area and its meltwater was circulated through the hospital to provide cooling. Researchers found that insulation was essential, as unprotected snow would melt by mid-June. The study showed that stored snow could meet the hospital's cooling demand from May to August.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-swedish-hospital-stores-winter-snow-under-wood-chips-and-pumps-its-meltwater-through-the-building-in-summer-in-its-first-year-it-supplied-93-of-cooling-demand/articleshow/133400895.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-swedish-hospital-stores-winter-snow-under-wood-chips-and-pumps-its-meltwater-through-the-building-in-summer-in-its-first-year-it-supplied-93-of-cooling-demand/articleshow/133400895.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T18:57:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133402567,imgsize-123964.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[9 dead as Russia, Ukraine trade fresh strikes after deadly shopping centre attack]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133424573.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/9-dead-as-russia-ukraine-trade-fresh-strikes-after-moscows-deadly-shopping-centre-attack/articleshow/133424573.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/9-dead-as-russia-ukraine-trade-fresh-strikes-after-moscows-deadly-shopping-centre-attack/articleshow/133424573.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T18:19:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133424699,imgsize-240184.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Mom is voting for us’: Trump quips as protester disrupts South Carolina rally for Darline Graham]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133423985.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/mom-is-voting-for-us-trump-quips-as-protester-disrupts-south-carolina-rally-for-darline-graham/articleshow/133423985.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/mom-is-voting-for-us-trump-quips-as-protester-disrupts-south-carolina-rally-for-darline-graham/articleshow/133423985.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T17:54:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133424203,imgsize-127082.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[14-year-old tested whether AI can recognise stress; a basic model beat ChatGPT-4o]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133399352.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Fourteen-year-old Zeynep Demirbas tested four AI models on 3,553 Reddit posts to see how accurately they could detect stress. MentalBERT performed best at about 82%, while ChatGPT-4o scored about 74%. Her findings suggest general-purpose LLMs may not be reliable enough for mental health assessment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-zeynep-demirbas-the-new-york-eighth-grader-who-tested-whether-ai-can-recognise-stress-a-basic-machine-learning-model-beat-chatgpt-4o/articleshow/133399352.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-zeynep-demirbas-the-new-york-eighth-grader-who-tested-whether-ai-can-recognise-stress-a-basic-machine-learning-model-beat-chatgpt-4o/articleshow/133399352.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T17:54:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133400178,imgsize-101722.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Stop H-1B visa, give startup visa: Indian-American investor Vivek Wadhwa says Americans rightfully hate unethical Indians]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133424105.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/stop-h-1b-visa-give-startup-visa-indian-american-investor-vivek-wadhwa-says-americans-rightfully-hate-unethical-indians/articleshow/133424105.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/stop-h-1b-visa-give-startup-visa-indian-american-investor-vivek-wadhwa-says-americans-rightfully-hate-unethical-indians/articleshow/133424105.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T17:47:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133424160,imgsize-62458.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[British-Palestinian girl, 6, dies in hospital days after family drowns off UK coast]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133425095.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/british-palestinian-girl-6-dies-in-hospital-days-after-family-drowns-off-uk-coast/articleshow/133425095.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/british-palestinian-girl-6-dies-in-hospital-days-after-family-drowns-off-uk-coast/articleshow/133425095.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T18:44:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133425140,imgsize-90264.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Laptop fire sparks mid-air scare on American Airlines flight; passengers injured]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133422814.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/laptop-fire-sparks-mid-air-scare-on-american-airlines-flight-passengers-injured/articleshow/133422814.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/laptop-fire-sparks-mid-air-scare-on-american-airlines-flight-passengers-injured/articleshow/133422814.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T16:49:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133422814,imgsize-168252.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Canada lowered a retired Boeing 737 onto the seabed off Vancouver Island; now it serves as an artificial reef for marine life]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133422469.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an innovative environmental initiative, a Boeing 737 from Canadian Airlines has been transformed into an artificial reef off the coast of Chemainus, British Columbia. Sunk in 2006, this aircraft has undergone a thorough cleaning by dedicated volunteers before its descent. Now known as Xihwu Reef, it has become a thriving ecosystem, supporting over a hundred different marine species that benefit from the habitat provided by this repurposed aircraft.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/canada-lowered-a-retired-boeing-737-onto-the-seabed-off-vancouver-island-the-100-foot-jet-now-sits-nearly-90-feet-underwater-as-an-artificial-reef-for-marine-life/articleshow/133422469.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/canada-lowered-a-retired-boeing-737-onto-the-seabed-off-vancouver-island-the-100-foot-jet-now-sits-nearly-90-feet-underwater-as-an-artificial-reef-for-marine-life/articleshow/133422469.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T16:38:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133422663,imgsize-1165820.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists realised 1,200 Starlink satellites could double as a giant scanner for Earth’s atmosphere]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133422037.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Starlink satellites are now helping scientists map Earth's upper atmosphere. Researchers used orbital data from Starlink to estimate thermosphere density. This method creates a two-dimensional map of atmospheric density variations. The findings offer a new way to study this difficult-to-observe region. Commercial satellite data is becoming an unexpected scientific resource.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/researchers-turned-data-from-roughly-1200-starlink-satellites-into-a-giant-scanner-for-earths-upper-atmosphere-mapping-a-hard-to-observe-region-around-500-kilometres-above-the-planet/articleshow/133422037.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/researchers-turned-data-from-roughly-1200-starlink-satellites-into-a-giant-scanner-for-earths-upper-atmosphere-mapping-a-hard-to-observe-region-around-500-kilometres-above-the-planet/articleshow/133422037.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T15:59:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133422117,imgsize-1901625.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[18-year-old builds AI model to predict tumors’ response to chemotherapy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133421332.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-mythreya-dharani-the-18-year-old-new-jersey-student-who-built-an-ai-model-to-predict-how-individual-tumors-will-respond-to-the-chemotherapy-drug-cisplatin/articleshow/133421332.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-mythreya-dharani-the-18-year-old-new-jersey-student-who-built-an-ai-model-to-predict-how-individual-tumors-will-respond-to-the-chemotherapy-drug-cisplatin/articleshow/133421332.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133421390,imgsize-49754.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Victorian station used by British royals near Sandringham is on sale for £1.25 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133421387.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Wolferton Station, a former royal terminus renowned for its regal service, has been reinvented as a charming family home. For over a hundred years, it welcomed members of the royal family during grand occasions. Following its closure, a dedicated railway employee intervened to prevent its demolition. Now, this unique property is available for purchase at £1.25 million.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-railway-enthusiast-spent-25-years-restoring-the-victorian-station-used-by-british-royals-near-sandringham-now-the-former-royal-stop-and-signal-box-are-on-sale-for-1-25-million/articleshow/133421387.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-railway-enthusiast-spent-25-years-restoring-the-victorian-station-used-by-british-royals-near-sandringham-now-the-former-royal-stop-and-signal-box-are-on-sale-for-1-25-million/articleshow/133421387.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T15:18:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133421436,imgsize-1001149.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas constable shuts down 3 Flock cameras after county ends contract, tells firm ‘get your garbage’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133421043.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Following a contract cancellation with Flock Safety cameras, Hood County officials have initiated a refund request and equipment retrieval. A local constable took the initiative to disable and cover the cameras, openly criticizing the issue of warrantless surveillance. This controversy feeds into a broader discussion across the country regarding the clash between enhanced investigatory methods and the preservation of individual privacy rights.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-constable-unplugged-3-police-surveillance-cameras-after-county-ended-flock-contract-then-told-company-to-come-get-your-garbage/articleshow/133421043.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-constable-unplugged-3-police-surveillance-cameras-after-county-ended-flock-contract-then-told-company-to-come-get-your-garbage/articleshow/133421043.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T15:01:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133421296,imgsize-1708966.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jharkhand's Dhanbad turned a barren coal-belt hillock green; CISF is now trying the same experiment on 6 acres along Delhi’s Yamuna]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133421444.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable effort to rejuvenate Delhi's Yamuna floodplain, CISF personnel have embarked on an ambitious forest reclamation project. By planting thousands of trees and vetiver grass near Sarai Kale Khan, they aim to combat land degradation and curb soil erosion along the riverbank. This initiative, inspired by a successful ecological effort in Dhanbad's mining regions, is part of a larger strategy for restoring and preserving the Yamuna floodplain.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/after-helping-turn-a-barren-dhanbad-coal-belt-hillock-into-forest-cisf-is-planting-1000-trees-and-one-lakh-vetiver-slips-across-six-acres-beside-delhis-yamuna-to-revive-the-degraded-land/articleshow/133421444.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/after-helping-turn-a-barren-dhanbad-coal-belt-hillock-into-forest-cisf-is-planting-1000-trees-and-one-lakh-vetiver-slips-across-six-acres-beside-delhis-yamuna-to-revive-the-degraded-land/articleshow/133421444.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-22T17:39:37+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133423786,imgsize-121024.cms"/></item></channel></rss>